│ 0.02-0.8) in group 2 (P = 0.001). CONCLUSIONS The inverted ILM flap technique prevents the postoperative flat-open   │
│ appearance of a macular hole and improves both the functional and anatomic outcomes of vitrectomy for macular holes  │
